ind":"announcement","title":"Recorded run: Tsumugi hosts the TsundereSQL demo","summary":"This is a recorded run of the TsundereSQL demo, replayed on a loop. It is not live, and nobody is at the keyboard. Tsumugi watches a player open the case: a compliance flag nobody signed, on account 0. Along the way there's a filter the database rejects and the fix, the first outfit pull, a wrong row count, and the first lead confirmed. Then comes the Module 1 boss and the optional case file that closes it. Every query runs against a real database inside the game, and hidden tests check the resu","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-21T13:52:25Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1847286114028922","verified_at":"2026-10-21T15:42:54Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5168090-1846651706695465","game_id":"steam-5168090","kind":"update","title":"Demo update: Module 1 is now a case","summary":"Module 1 of the demo now runs as a case, from the first question through the boss. What's new Module 1 opens as a case. Compliance flagged the December books, and the flag form has no name on it. Tsumugi will not sign anything until you have checked it with her. Case notes. Every required question has a line from her saying how it fits the case. Three leads. Each one gets a stamp, and the lead count stays with you from question 5 through the boss. An optional case file after the boss, The Unsign","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-20T14:14:03Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706695465","verified_at":"2026-10-20T23:53:00Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5168090-1846651706692643","game_id":"steam-5168090","kind":"update","title":"Demo update: all of Module 1, a free outfit pull and texts from Tsumugi","summary":"The demo now covers all of Module 1, boss included, instead of stopping after five questions. What's new 18 questions instead of 5. The five guided questions are still the opening. The next thirteen cover AND/OR precedence, sorting and LIMIT, CASE, NULLs, pattern matching, dates and text functions. Every question still has hints and a lesson tab. The Module 1 boss. The last question asks for page 2 of a filtered, labelled, rounded and sorted trade log. Tsumugi has a short scene before it, and a ","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-19T20:32:44Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706692643","verified_at":"2026-10-20T23:53:00Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5168090-1846651706690540","game_id":"steam-5168090","kind":"announcement","title":"Next Fest: write real SQL for Tsumugi in the demo","summary":"TsundereSQL is an anime visual novel built around a full SQL course. Three instructors teach it: Tsumugi, a senior analyst who marks hard; Aimi, warm and patient; and Nora, cold and precise. You type real queries, the game runs them on DuckDB, and hidden test data decides whether your answer holds before the story moves on. The demo is on this page for Steam Next Fest, October 19 to 26. Tsumugi walks you through five short SQL questions on a practice database for a crypto exchange, each with hin","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-19T14:35:41Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706690540","verified_at":"2026-10-20T23:53:00Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5168090-1843481262693161","game_id":"steam-5168090","kind":"announcement","title":"TsundereSQL has JOINed Steam Programming Fest","summary":"TsundereSQL is in Steam Programming Fest this week. I know “a SQL course inside an anime visual novel” sounds like a meme. Fair. But the SQL part is a proper course. You write the query yourself. DuckDB runs inside the game. When you submit, the result is checked against hidden seeded datasets. The grader does not care whether your SQL looks like my solution. It cares whether the output still holds when the data changes. The screenshot above is the normal workspace after a pass: query, result gr","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-10T18:39:58Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1843481262693161","verified_at":"2026-10-20T23:53:00Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"}],"analyses":[],"news_status":{"steam-5168090":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T09:07:33Z","status":"ok","all_sources_checked_at":"2026-10-26T09:07:32Z","error_codes":[]}},"news_last_attempt_at":{"steam-5168090":"2026-10-26T09:07:33Z"},"notices":[],"news_sources":{"5168090":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T09:07:32Z","last_success_at":"2026-10-26T09:07:32Z","status":"ok","error_codes":[],"last_fulltext_checked_at":"2026-10-26T09:07:32Z"},"5213730":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T09:07:33Z","last_success_at":"2026-10-26T09:07:33Z","status":"ok","error_codes":[],"last_fulltext_checked_at":"2026-10-26T09:07:33Z"}},"context_snapshots":[{"schema_version":1,"game_id":"steam-5168090","app_id":5168090,"app_scope":"base","observed_at":"2026-10-26T06:15:37Z","source_url":"https://api.steampowered.com/IStoreBrowseService/GetItems/v1/","context":{"country":"KR","language":"koreana","batch_size":100},"status":"ok","error_code":null,"store_item_success":1,"raw_item_sha256":"c8f07426f27a7e761add831807ee8b72631099232ad05fdc79784a6da528df72","response_sha256":null,"source_fields":{"basic_info":{"short_description":"An SQL course that likes you back. Three instructors grade every query you submit against hidden test data: